# Go gRPC Docker Standards

## Base Image Selection

- **Build stage**: Use `golang:1.22-alpine`
- **Runtime stage**: Use `alpine:3.19` (Go compiles to a static binary — no runtime needed)

## Multi-Stage Dockerfile Pattern

```dockerfile
# Build stage
FROM golang:1.22-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app

# Install dependencies first (layer cache)
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN go mod download

# Build static binary
COPY . .
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux go build -ldflags="-s -w" -o server ./cmd/server

# Runtime stage (minimal)
FROM alpine:3.19
WORKDIR /app

# CA certs for TLS (gRPC often uses TLS in production)
RUN apk --no-cache add ca-certificates

# Non-root user
RUN adduser -D -g '' appuser
USER appuser

COPY --from=builder /app/server .

# gRPC default port
EXPOSE 50051

# gRPC health probe (Kubernetes standard for gRPC services)
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=10s --retries=3 \
  CMD ["/app/server", "-healthcheck"] || exit 1

CMD ["./server"]
```

## Key gRPC-Specific Settings

### Static Binary (Required for Alpine)

```dockerfile
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux go build -ldflags="-s -w" -o server ./cmd/server
```

- `CGO_ENABLED=0`: no C library dependencies — required for alpine/scratch
- `GOOS=linux`: cross-compile if building on macOS
- `-s -w`: strip symbol table and DWARF info (~30% smaller binary)

### gRPC Port Convention

gRPC services default to port `50051`. Document deviations.

## Kubernetes Health Probes for gRPC

Use `grpc-health-probe` (or Kubernetes native gRPC probe, k8s 1.24+):

```yaml
# Kubernetes 1.24+ native gRPC probe
livenessProbe:
  grpc:
    port: 50051
  initialDelaySeconds: 10
  periodSeconds: 15

readinessProbe:
  grpc:
    port: 50051
  initialDelaySeconds: 5
  periodSeconds: 10
```

For older clusters, use `grpc-health-probe` binary in the container:

```dockerfile
# Add grpc-health-probe to image
RUN wget -qO/bin/grpc_health_probe https://github.com/grpc-ecosystem/grpc-health-probe/releases/download/v0.4.19/grpc_health_probe-linux-amd64 \
    && chmod +x /bin/grpc_health_probe
```

## docker-compose for Local Development

```yaml
services:
  grpc-server:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "50051:50051"
    environment:
      - GRPC_REFLECTION=true
      - DB_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@db:5432/appdb?sslmode=disable
    depends_on:
      db:
        condition: service_healthy

  db:
    image: postgres:16-alpine
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: appdb
      POSTGRES_USER: postgres
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: postgres
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U postgres"]
      interval: 5s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5
```

## .dockerignore for Go gRPC Projects

```
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum
gen/
*.pb.go
```

Note: if committing generated proto files, remove `gen/` and `*.pb.go` from .dockerignore.

## Development vs Production

### Development (with hot reload via air)

```yaml
services:
  grpc-server:
    build:
      context: .
      dockerfile: Dockerfile.dev
    volumes:
      - .:/app
    ports:
      - "50051:50051"
    environment:
      - GRPC_REFLECTION=true
```

**Dockerfile.dev:**

```dockerfile
FROM golang:1.22-alpine
WORKDIR /app
RUN go install github.com/cosmtrek/air@latest
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN go mod download
CMD ["air"]
```

### Production

```yaml
services:
  grpc-server:
    build: .
    # No volume mount — static binary, immutable image
    environment:
      - GRPC_REFLECTION=false
```
